---
import ScholarlyLayout from '../layouts/ScholarlyLayout.astro';
import SiteMap from '../components/SiteMap.jsx';
import sites from '../data/sites.json';
import iamata from '../data/iamata.json';
import cases from '../data/epidemics-cases.json';
import photos from '../data/photos.json';
---
<ScholarlyLayout title="Interactive Map">
  <p class="eyebrow">Fieldwork · Map</p>
  <h1>Interactive Map [WIP]</h1>
  <p>
    [PLACEHOLDER: short intro to the map's purpose.] The map shows two kinds of place:
    the sites visited in July–August 2026 (solid markers, each linked to its Field
    Journal entry), and places known only from the texts (hollow markers): the home
    towns of the petitioners in the Epidaurian iamata, and the towns where the
    Hippocratic <em>Epidemics</em> are set. Use the buttons to switch each layer on or
    off, and click a marker for what is recorded there. The argument the map supports is
    on <a href="/geographies">Two Geographies of Healing</a>.
  </p>
  <SiteMap client:only="react" sites={sites} iamata={iamata} cases={cases} photos={photos} />
</ScholarlyLayout>
